cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PsyStat in your research, please cite it as below, and also cite the statistical methods you used."
title: "PsyStat: A statistical analysis application for psychology and the social sciences"
type: software
version: 1.2.0
date-released: 2026-11-01
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/terysetn02-source/psystat"
url: "https://github.com/terysetn02-source/psystat"
abstract: >-
  PsyStat is a free, open-source desktop application with a graphical interface for statistical analysis in
  psychology and the social sciences. It offers data management, descriptive and inferential statistics, ANOVA,
  regression, mediation, exploratory and confirmatory factor analysis, structural equation modeling, psychometric
  network analysis, power analysis and Bayesian analysis, with APA-style output.
authors:
  - family-names: Setiawan
    given-names: Tery
    affiliation: "Universitas Kristen Maranatha; Radboud University"
keywords:
  - statistics
  - psychology
  - social science
  - structural equation modeling
  - network analysis
  - Bayesian analysis
  - desktop application
